# Vadhyar browser stack and evidence rules

- Current status: all M0 gates accepted at the human stability stop; no app writer, M1+ deferred. Only root finishes previously requested protected GitHub sync/records; no automatic continuation.
- Root alone may finish the previously requested GitHub cleanup/sync after stability acceptance, through normal branch/required-CI protections. No release/tag replacement or history rewrite.
- The product follows one trusted local project; prepared native demos are historical, not a current requirement.
- Use React, strict TypeScript, the existing esbuild/Vitest stack, Zod contracts and the official OpenAI SDK; keep one pinned npm lockfile.
- The host listens on loopback and owns root/project identity, Host/Origin/session validation, metadata, source captures and check execution.
- Host-issued source IDs resolve only to allowlisted real paths and valid current line spans.
- Browser records stay local to the profile/origin; keep original predictions, attempts and source identities.
- Validate async operation identity and reject stale/late responses; failed reads/saves preserve valid work.
- Preview bounded excerpts and obtain explicit consent before optional provider transmission. Never expose keys in browser data or child processes.
- Interpretations and static links are proposals, not runtime evidence or requirement verdicts.
- Project checks require separate consent; use eligible existing scripts, fixed invocation, no implicit npm hooks, bounded redacted output and timeouts.
- Trusted project commands are not sandboxed. Keep command outcomes, freshness and self-reported verdicts separate.
- Preserve dirty-buffer guards, cancellation, acknowledgement, storage conflict/reset invalidation and export recovery.
- Render model output safely without executable links or HTML; the teacher has no edit or shell tools.
- Keep reading captures version-bound and view-local; support explicit export before leaving.
- Do not claim mastery, authorship or learning gains from activity or rehearsed developer fixtures.
- Build and package in isolated copies; do not rebuild shared assets or reload another user's active session.
- Preserve upstream mappings, copyright/license texts and exact release evidence; old paths resolve through docs/history.md.
